6. Host-driven physical HTTP test result
----------------------------------------

The Windows test client was run against 192.168.2.2:80 while the PA-220
foreground service was active. The separate client log records:

  GET /api/board       -> 200
  GET /                -> 200
  GET /api/status      -> 200
  GET /api/memory      -> 200
  GET /api/network     -> 200
  GET /not-found       -> 404
  POST /api/status     -> 405
  RST/abort exercise followed by successful GET /api/status -> 200

Client summary:
  SUMMARY PASS cases=8 rst_recovery=PASS

Packet-analysis qualification:
The abort-test TCP connection (client source port 5950) completed its
handshake, then the client sent FIN before sending any HTTP request payload.
The server returned HTTP 400; the client then sent RST+ACK. A new connection
(source port 5951) subsequently sent GET /api/status and received HTTP 200.
Accordingly, this evidence demonstrates reset/close handling followed by
successful new-connection service; it does NOT demonstrate an RST interrupting
a partially transmitted HTTP request.

7. Safety / operation boundary
------------------------------

The reported test used a RAM-loaded Stage-3 image. No flash, saveenv, CPLD
write, SPI/eMMC/NAND write, reset, reboot, or power-cycle was part of the
reported HTTP test. The BIN is a Cavium OCTEON PA-220 Stage-3 image and must
not be treated as a generic firmware-upgrade image.

